      "description": "TSV tables compared by the full record grid PLUS the trailing-newline and line-ending choices as normative fields. Differs from the base `semantic-tabular-v1` profile only in that `trailingNewline` and `lineTerminator` are NOT ignored: this subset's vocabulary declares `set-trailing-newline` and `set-line-ending` as real mutation kinds that genuinely rewrite bytes (IANA TSV has no header/data distinction to make substantive the way RFC 4180's `has_header` convention does, so its own real serialization concerns fill that role instead), and they have to actually participate in the comparison or those scenarios are no-ops.",
